WorkItem.Description:
SpecSharp2 incorrectly binds names to private inherited fields that should be inaccessible.  This allows incorrect programs to be accepted.  For example, the following is compiled without error -

    public class Base { public int pblc; }
    public class Derived : Base { private float prvt; }
    public sealed class MoreDerived : Derived { }
    public static class Program  {
        public static void Main(string[] args) {
            MoreDerived m = new MoreDerived();
            m.prvt = 0.42F; // Should be error: Base.prvt is inaccessible.
        }
    }

Also correct programs may be rejected, as in this version of the above snippet -

    public class Base  {  public int pblc;  }
    public class Derived : Base  {  new private float pblc; // obscures Base.pblc;  }
    public sealed class MoreDerived : Derived { // Base.pblc should be accessible again.  }
    public static class Program  {
        public static void Main(string[] args) {
            MoreDerived m = new MoreDerived();
            int foo = m.pblc; // Should bind to Base.pblc, specsharp2 gives type error.
        }
    }
